<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  White theme page background, and the anchor for the whole theme's tonal scale.

  The page is the lightest surface and everything else steps down from it, which is the
  Black theme's arrangement inverted: there the page is the darkest thing and surfaces
  step up. Keeping the direction consistent is what makes the two themes feel like the
  same app rather than two designs.

  Scale, all measured against this page:

    page    #F7F9FB   1.00
    surface #ECEFF4   1.09   nav, dropdowns, search
    card    #EAEEF3   1.10   cards, transactions, keypad
    input   #DDE3EB   1.22   fields, icon tiles
    border  #CCD4DF   1.42   every stroke

  Widest step is 1.42:1; Black's is 1.49:1. Was 19.2:1 when cards carried a black
  outline. Keep new surfaces inside that band.

  The gradient is almost flat on purpose. The previous one ran #FFFFFF to #E2E8F0, a
  range wide enough that a card could be lighter than the page at the top of a screen and
  darker at the bottom, so the hierarchy inverted as you scrolled.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <gradient
        android:startColor="#F7F9FB"
        android:centerColor="#F5F7FA"
        android:endColor="#F2F5F8"
        android:angle="270"
        android:type="linear"/>
</shape>
